WEBVTT

00:00:01.244 --> 00:00:03.604
Every video starts
as words.

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:05.420
In this studio,
the words come

00:00:05.994 --> 00:00:08.404
first. The voice you
are hearing was read

00:00:08.404 --> 00:00:10.980
by an open model,
and the studio knows

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.140
the moment each
word is spoken.

00:00:13.544 --> 00:00:14.660
That timing drives

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.760
everything.
The captions below

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.404
are built from it,
two lines at a time,

00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:22.344
and each word lights
up as it is said.

00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:24.944
Visuals land
on their words too.

00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:26.600
When I say contrast,
a title

00:00:27.484 --> 00:00:29.160
appears, and it
stays on its word

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.244
even
if the take changes.

00:00:31.244 --> 00:00:33.350
The music steps back
while I speak, and

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.844
comes forward
in the pauses.

00:00:35.844 --> 00:00:37.500
Before a render,
the studio

00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:39.140
checks every frame.

00:00:39.444 --> 00:00:41.350
Text sits inside
the safe zone, big

00:00:41.984 --> 00:00:43.520
enough to read,
with a contrast

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.584
of at least four
and a half to one,

00:00:45.584 --> 00:00:48.244
and it stays long
enough to finish.

00:00:48.244 --> 00:00:50.784
After the render,
it measures the file

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.644
itself.

00:00:51.644 --> 00:00:53.744
Loudness lands
at minus fourteen,

00:00:53.744 --> 00:00:55.420
with no flashes
and no frozen

00:00:56.284 --> 00:00:57.230
frames. Nothing

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.080
here was checked
by eye alone.

